You walk along the animal trail pretty fast. It's quite easy; you don't even have to move branches apart. You are surrounded by short bushes, richly studded with white flowers. They are so numerous that you can hardly see the leaves. Their smell is rather nice.

You are almost halfway to your destination. Thickets become denser. Actually, you see some new plants. These are short, one-meter-high bushes, with beautiful lilac flowers. A pleasant sweetish smell is coming from them. It's strange, but there is almost no grass near these bushes. The bushes with white flowers form a rather dense living wall, with lilac bushes growing quite sparsely. You need to decide whether to thread your way through the thickets of white bushes or try to go through the lilac ones.